'''''Dioon califanoi''''' is a [[species]] of [[cycad]] that is native to [[Oaxaca]] and [[Puebla]] states, [[Mexico]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tropicos.org/Name/9600172|title= Dioon califanoi in Tropicos}}</ref> It is found near [[Teotitlán del Camino]] and [[Huautla de Jiménez]].<ref name="iucn status 20 November 2021"/>
[[image:Flickr - brewbooks - Cycads in the greenhouse - Paloma gardens (1).jpg|thumb|left|250px|With cones in a greenhouse at Paloma Gardens, New Zealand]]

==Mutualism==
{{See also|Pharaxonotha#Association with cycads}}
The beetle ''[[Pharaxonotha bicolor]]'' is in an obligatory [[Mutualism (biology)|mutualistic]] relationship with ''Dioon califanoi'', living and breeding in male cones and consuming pollen and cone tissues while serving as a pollinating vector by transferring pollen to female cones.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Skelley |first1=Paul |last2=Tang |first2=William |last3=Pérez-Farrera |first3=Miguel |date=February 24, 2022 |title=Review of Pharaxonotha Reitter (Coleoptera: Erotylidae: Pharaxonothinae) inhabiting the cycad genus Dioon Lindl. (Cycadales), with descriptions of nine new species and comments on P. kirschii Reitter |url=https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/insectamundi/1413 |journal=Insecta Mundi |pages=3, 6}}</ref>

